# CSE450 Translation of Programming Languages
## Lecture 4 : Symbol Tables
---
### Symbol Tables
...
- A **{{color=orange|symbol table}}** is a data structure that associates identifiers (names) with the user-defined data they refer to.
...
- Programming languages have many kinds of symbols:
...
    - {{color=id|Variables}}
...
    - {{color=id|Function names}}
...
    - {{color=id|Constants}}
...
    - {{color=id|Template names}}
...
- Other programs may have {{color=yellow|position labels}}, {{color=magenta|user-defined types}}, {{color=cyan|enumerations}}, etc.
---
[title] ### Symbol Table Example
